<p><code>pop-http</code> covers both directions of HTTP. The server half — the inbound request and the response you send
back — is in <a href="/basics/requests-responses">Requests &amp; Responses</a>. This page is the outbound half: calling
somebody else's API from inside your application. <code>Pop\Http\Client</code> wraps curl or PHP streams behind one
interface, and adds authentication, middleware, promises and a mock handler for tests.</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
